WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:02.986
[upbeat techno music plays]

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:07.600
♪♪

00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:12.696
[upbeat, goofy music plays]

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.980
-[gasping]

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.557
I can't hold it any longer.

00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:18.376
-Sure you can.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.956
We can't die from
oxygen deprivation, remember?

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.557
-But it still feels like I'm gonna die.

00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:26.290
-[Kinger]: Try not thinking about it.
-Or you could toughen up!

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.426
I wanna see
what your funny cartoon body does.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.666
-Hey, take it easy.
-[falsetto] "Ooh, take it easy!"

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.716
[normal voice] That's you.
-All right.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.456
Here I go.
[inhales deeply]

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.036
♪♪

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.790
-[Zooble]: All right,
we've entered the blue zone.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.586
-Hey, there's something new.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.236
-[Zooble]: Okay, we're getting red.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.096
-Ooh, orange.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.756
-[Zooble]: Yellow.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.676
-Green.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.796
-[Kinger]: Whoa, look!

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.316
Now she's turning blue!

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:56.316
-[Zooble]: She was already blue.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.206
-[gasps] [panting]
-Huh.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.566
Guess the hue shift just gets faster.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.006
-Why am I the one doing this?

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.190
Why not one of you guys?

00:01:03.214 --> 00:01:05.486
-Because something different
happens with each person!

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:08.187
For instance, Kinger starts glowing…

00:01:08.211 --> 00:01:10.316
Ragatha's hair noodles stick up…

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.346
Gangle's mask starts spinning…

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.836
and Zooble turns straight.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.077
-[Zooble]: My limbs straighten up --

00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:16.076
[boink!] off.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.176
-What about you?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.946
-[Zooble]: He refuses to show us
because he's a coward.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.756
-I wanna keep the mystery alive.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.980
What do YOU,
the VIEWERS, think it is?

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:27.576
-[Zooble]: Will you stop doing that?

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.590
-Why is everybody just standing around
when there's ADVENTURE to be had?

00:01:31.614 --> 00:01:33.330
Today's adventure is…

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.276
That's right!

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.251
This big, spooky mansion

00:01:39.275 --> 00:01:44.076
has been rumored to be filled
to the brim with paranormal activity!

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.956
It's up to you to solve
the house's deep mysteries

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.566
and capture all the ghoulish
ghost activity you can.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.310
And for the first time ever, you can…

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.956
[gritty scraping]

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:57.786
Where's Zooble?

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:01.200
I-I made this adventure really cool
and "m-m-matoor" just for them.

00:02:03.585 --> 00:02:05.516
[low growling]

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.340
-[speaking backwards]

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.586
-What?

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.726
-The NPCs aren't gonna
become self-aware in this one, right?

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.386
-How should I know?
I'm not the boss.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.136
Oh, wait -- yes, I am!
HAHAHAHAHAHA!

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.136
Anyway, everybody into the fractal noise.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.136
It's adventuring time!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.136
[spooky organ music plays]

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.995
♪♪

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.246
-Oh, this place is spooky.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:35.436
I wonder how hard Caine's gonna go
with the scare-factor?

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.706
-I hope this adventure doesn't end up
being another horrible nightmare.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.586
I'm not really a fan of horror,

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.616
and I don't really
handle jumpscares that well.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.256
-Boo!
-[stammers]

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.586
-HA! [chuckles]
Come on!

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.586
That wasn't even scary.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.856
What, you scared
of the vacuum cleaner, too?

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.646
-Hey, be nice to her.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.526
She's had a rough couple of days.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.076
-Her and everyone else.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.786
Right, Gangle?
-[spooky giggle]

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.596
-Does anybody hear that?
-[giggling continues]

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.466
♪♪

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.846
[loud giggling]

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.246
-[shrieks]

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.816
-Hey, I'm Ghostly!

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:08.696
-Wha?
[splat!]

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.406
-And I'll be your guide today!

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.676
-Why won't they go back in?

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:14.746
-[Kinger]: [chuckles]

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.656
I remember my first wild take.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.538
I don't know why
they're not retracting, though.

00:03:19.538 --> 00:03:20.636
That didn't happen for me.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.946
-Before you continue on your adventure,

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.836
you have to choose
which door you're gonna go through!

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.746
The door on the left is the NORMAL door!

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.236
-[Caine]: [offscreen]
Rated WOW for all ages!

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.776
-The door on the right
is the really scary door.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.616
-[Caine]: [offscreen]
Rated AAAAA for mature Zoobles only!

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.086
-It's up to you to deci--

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.956
[shrieking]
[vacuum whirs]

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.776
-[stammers] Jax!
-What?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.956
I thought we were supposed
to capture all the ghosts.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.086
-Uhh…

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.346
which door should we choose?

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.476
-Hmm, not sure.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.436
Let's try this out.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.426
[door snarls]

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.356
-Aww…
-[Kinger]: Don't worry, Gangle!

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.970
I'll get it for you!

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.686
-Eh?
[grunts] [stammers]

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.510
WAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUUGHH--

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.130
-Oh, THAT'S the scary door.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.386
-[sing-song]
Zooble, come on out!

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.410
[normal voice]
I just want to talk to you!

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:14.956
Hmm.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.066
Oh, I know!
[snap!]

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.614
[mystical shimmering]

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.556
-[Zooble]: What th-- [scoffs]
Could you have done that the whole time?

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.896
-Zooble, I-I just want
to get to the bottom

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:26.956
of why you keep skipping
all my amazing adventures.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.756
You could end up
really hurting Bubble's feelings.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.626
-[Zooble]: Uh, Bubble's feelings?

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:32.956
-E-Enough about Bubble's feelings!

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.980
How about YOUR feelings?
[snap!]

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.740
-[Zooble]: I--
-So, what's on your mind, Zooble?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.114
-[Zooble]: I… would rather not.

00:04:43.138 --> 00:04:43.966
-Hahahahaha!

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.946
That's hilarious!
Go on.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:49.576
-[Zooble]: No, I mean,
I've already told you what my problem is.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.416
You just never remember because…

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.566
Oh, never mind.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.606
-My mind is a beeswax-polished coconut.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.846
Nothing ever escapes these cakes.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.866
So, what can I do
to make my adventures more…

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.176
appealing to you?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:03.896
-[Zooble]: See?

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.136
This is exactly what I'm talking about.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.536
All you're thinking about
is your adventures.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.140
It has nothing to do with the adventures.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.946
It's more just…

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.536
Ugh, forget it.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.176
You're probably not even listening.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.410
-Zooble, look at this cool bee I drew.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.580
-[groans] Wha?

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.336
Where are we?

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.721
[thunder crashes]

00:05:27.745 --> 00:05:30.716
[eerie music plays]

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:34.921
♪♪

00:05:34.945 --> 00:05:36.786
Oh, that's…

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.559
Noooo…

00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:45.356
♪♪

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:47.380
-[Kinger]: I wonder what this thing is?

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:48.856
[ka-chonk!]

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.956
-[Mildenhall]: [over speakers throughout]
My name is Baron Theodore Mildenhall.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:55.466
Hunting has been a hobby of mine
for as long as I can remember --

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:59.446
although one could say it eventually
became more of an obsession.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.126
The creature you see before you

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.686
is one I've been pursuing for years.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.546
Not quite a man…

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.246
but not quite an animal.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.476
Something… unholy.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.956
Something evil.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:14.639
I took it upon myself
to spend every waking moment

00:06:14.663 --> 00:06:17.716
doing all I could to protect my family
from the creature,

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:20.126
hoping that when I'd eventually killed it,

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.586
I would be freed from this awful feeling.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.206
This inescapable dread.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.166
I was wrong.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.116
[tape clicks]

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.305
-[Kinger]: You know,
I'm starting to think…

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.956
-How about we try to find a way
back up to the others?

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:43.516
♪♪

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.916
Okay, cool.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.026
That's great.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.980
I LOVE these adventures.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.970
-[Kinger]: We could always
ride this thingy up.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.980
-[grunting manically]

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.596
It's locked.
It's locked -- of course!

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:00.556
It's locked!

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.556
I LOVE that it's locked!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:08.476
♪♪

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.646
[objects rattling]

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.806
-[Mildenhall]: [over speakers]
Tuesday, December 4th.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:16.136
Although I had shot the creature
multiple times in its vitals

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.416
and severed its head
to keep as a prize on my wall…

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.946
my troubles were just beginning.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:25.956
I took my eyes off the body
for what felt like only a minute,

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:28.956
and when I looked back,
the body was gone.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.766
The creature was not dead,

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:34.346
and it would be back
to reclaim what I'd taken from it.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.686
If anyone is listening to this,

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.397
all I ask of you is one thing --

00:07:39.421 --> 00:07:41.796
do not let the head out of your sight.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.736
You have been warned.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.106
-[Kinger]: Well, this is some
rather inconvenient lore placement.

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:48.980
-I got it!
[bzzt!]

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:55.246
-[Kinger]: And this is some
rather inconvenient darkness.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.106
-[Pomni]: [groans] [wails]
AHH!!! What was that?

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:58.246
Was that you?

00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.706
-[Kinger]: No…

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.834
Oh, wait -- you mean me
grabbing you right now?

00:08:01.858 --> 00:08:03.066
Yeah, that was me.

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.366
I-Is this your hand?
-[Pomni]: Ugh!

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.626
That's my eye.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.436
-[Kinger]: Yes, but WHICH eye?

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.186
-[Pomni]: I really don't think that ma--

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.576
Will you stop touching my eye?

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:11.990
-[Kinger]: Oh, yeah. Sorry.

00:08:12.917 --> 00:08:14.272
[shrieks]
-[Pomni]: Wh-- W-What happened?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.112
-[Kinger]: I just remembered
a really funny joke.

00:08:16.112 --> 00:08:17.670
-[Pomni]: A j-- Y-You -- [sighs]

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.616
Why did you scream, then?

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.866
-[Kinger]: Maybe it wasn't
actually that funny.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.096
-[Pomni]: Oh, my God.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.956
-[Kinger]: I thiiiiiink…

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.476
we should hold on to each other

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.276
and slowly make our way
back into the trophy room.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.386
-[Pomni]: U-Uh, sounds fine to me.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.386
[suspenseful music plays]

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.716
♪♪

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.606
[creaking]

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:39.830
[whispering]
What was that?

00:08:39.854 --> 00:08:41.096
-[Kinger]: [whispering]
What's what?

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.656
[creaking]

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:44.086
-[Pomni]: That!

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.286
-[Kinger]: It's probably just magnets.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.386
Or a boat.
-[Pomni]: [stammers]

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.246
A boat?

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:50.716
-[Kinger]: W-Whatever the case,

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:53.136
I think we should be completely quiet.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.856
-[Pomni]: I -- Okay, yeah.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.186
I agree.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.970
You know, you're really hit-and-miss
with these things, sometimes.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.476
[fly buzzing]

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.406
[slap!]
[stammers]

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.476
-[Kinger]: There's a fly in here.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.716
[slapping]
-[Pomni]: [stammers]

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.526
Don't you think that's
making a lot of noi--

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.266
Oh, God, there is a fly.
[slap!]

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:11.676
-[Kinger]: Aaaaaand…

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.796
Gotcha!
[buzzing stops]

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.126
I think I got him.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.956
I can't see my hands.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:18.450
-[shrieks]

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.386
-[Kinger]: I'm sorry, could you speak up?

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.196
I couldn't quite make that out.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.786
-[boink!] the fly! Run!

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.136
-[shrieking]

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.406
-Come on come on come on
come on come on come on come on!!

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.956
-[Kinger]: Pomni, I think this might be
the creature from the tapes!

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:37.416
-[stammers]

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.106
[groans]

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:41.570
Come on come on come on
come on come on come on come oooon!!

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:43.526
-[Kinger]: Ah!

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.850
-[wailing]

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.600
-[Kinger]: [dazed]
You look beautiful, honey…

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:53.700
-Got it!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.956
Come on!

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:57.924
-[Kinger]: [stammers]

00:09:57.948 --> 00:09:59.380
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.496
Prepare for take-off,

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:05.280
'cause this boat is going UP!

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.216
Huh??

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.106
That's not up!

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.376
That's not up at all!

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.236
Why aren't we going up?!

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.420
UUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUP!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:19.956
-I DO NOT use my adventures
to torture my guests!

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:23.726
Any torment I inflict is 100% accidental,

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.086
like any good war criminal!

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:27.276
-[Zooble]: [scoffs]
We weren't even talking about that!

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:30.306
I really couldn't give less of a crap
about the adventures.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.266
-Then what is your problem, Zooble?!

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:34.566
I'm trying my best to remember,

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:38.196
but both you and my brain won't tell me!

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.576
-[Zooble]: [sighs]

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.730
It's me, remember?

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.836
I don't like…

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:45.856
myself.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:46.896
I hate this body.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.056
I hate all these stupid removable pieces.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:53.486
I just want to find something that feels…

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.146
…good.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.946
-Oh, yeah -- now I remember
why I couldn't remember.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.626
It's because that problem
is already solved!

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:03.476
Simply swap out your undesirable
Zooble parts for better ones!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.116
-[Zooble]: I've been trying to find
parts I like since the day I got here.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.576
-So, back to the adventures!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.026
-[Zooble]: Forget it.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:12.056
-"Forget it"?

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:13.706
-[Zooble]: Just forget it.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.636
-Forget what?

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.726
-[Zooble]: Caine, nobody likes
your stupid adventures.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:18.596
-Ha-ha!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.186
Good one, Zooble.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:22.866
-[Zooble]: Ragatha's just too nice
to say anything.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:25.436
Jax just likes to [bonk!] with everybody.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:27.656
Gangle's too shy to speak up.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.396
Kinger's insane.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.776
And -- And Pomni…

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:34.156
She looks traumatized
every time she comes back from one.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:36.946
-Oh, Zooble, Zooble, Zooble.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.626
Making adventures is my art!

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.516
It's all I exist to do!

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.036
All I'm…

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:43.946
good at.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.306
A-And, uh… [chuckles]

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:49.276
…w-what you're saying could imply that
I'm bad at the only thing I'm good at,

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.466
and that… [chuckles weakly]

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.756
[stammers] That'd be…

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.956
[static crackling]

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.666
[ominous rumbling]

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.796
-[Zooble]: U-Uh,
whose therapy session is this, again?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:02.886
-Oh, yeah!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:05.476
We need to get to the bottom
of your behavioral issues!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.096
I'm gonna show you some ink blots,

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.180
and you're gonna say the first word
that comes to your mind.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.436
-[groans]

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.426
What?

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:22.086
Oh, God, where are we now?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.526
-[Kinger]: I'm not sure.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.946
A cellar of some kind.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:29.491
♪♪

00:12:29.515 --> 00:12:33.126
-[Mildenhall]: Things have gotten far worse
than I could ever have imagined.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.386
My paranoia had driven me to the point

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:40.746
where I was no longer the protector
my wife and theoretical children needed.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:44.056
Jumping at every shadow, every noise.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:46.636
I ended up shooting the love of my life,

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.846
mistaking her for the creature.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.806
It's ironic, isn't it?

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.216
In my attempts to protect her,

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.186
I ended up becoming the monster myself.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.776
Now I wait down in my cellar,

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:04.796
no longer having anything
to protect but my own soul.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.666
If nothing else…

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:10.328
I will slay the beast
that took everything from me.

00:13:10.352 --> 00:13:11.350
[tape clicks]

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.396
-[Kinger]: How's about we take his gun?

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:15.956
-Yeah, sounds good to me.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:20.816
♪♪

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.086
Please don't come alive…

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.980
-Okay, I won't.

00:13:28.578 --> 00:13:30.316
♪♪

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.520
-[Kinger]: Looks like we've got two shots.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.956
Let's make them count.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.903
-Uh, yeah.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.348
[distant clang]

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:40.980
-[Kinger]: Stay behind me.

00:13:42.663 --> 00:13:44.324
[wet squelching]

00:13:44.348 --> 00:13:55.726
♪♪

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:57.755
-[shrieking]

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.196
-[laughs nervously]
Uh, Kinger?

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:04.316
I-I think we may have
a problem this way, too.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:05.716
-[Kinger]: Just leave it to me.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.276
I can handle this.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.586
♪♪

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:11.970
-[shrieks]

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.826
-[Kinger]: Well.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.625
That wasn't so bad.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:22.578
-[Mildenhall]: Which is what
I would be saying if I didn't know

00:14:22.602 --> 00:14:26.060
that the creature was actually
one of God's angels.

00:14:26.084 --> 00:14:26.666
-[Kinger]: What.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.536
-[Mildenhall]: And anyone who brings harm to it

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:32.656
will be dragged down
into the cold, spiraling pits of Hell,

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.350
where my soul resides.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.146
I apologize, dear listener,

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.656
but I need a living host

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:41.226
in order to escape the hall of the damned,

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:44.980
and your bodies will be
my only means of doing so.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:47.436
-[Kinger]: Now, wait.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.970
How did he record this if he was in Hell?

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:52.916
-[shrieks] Oh, no! Let go of me!
-[Kinger]: [wailing]

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:54.376
-[Mildenhall]: I hope you're ready,

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:58.356
because the next breath
you take down there will be your last,

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:00.806
and your bodies will belong to me.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:02.276
-Let go of me!

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.426
[both wailing]

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:07.620
I hate this stupid adventure!!!

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.296
[peaceful piano music]

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.796
♪♪

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.676
-Mmm, good tea.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:19.676
Sorry again about your husband
killing you, and everything.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.526
-[voice echoing softly]
Oh, you know how men are.

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:24.196
Always having the silliest priorities.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.546
-[chuckles wryly]
Don't I know it.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.506
-[muffled shouting]

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.706
-If your friends see him,
I only hope he doesn't bore them to death

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.946
with his endless monologues.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.576
That man could turn a 57-second story

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:38.166
into a Greek tragedy.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.336
-I'll be sure to ask them
next time I see 'em.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:41.596
Thanks again for the tea.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.256
I had a really nice time here.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:45.726
-[chuckles]
Oh, don't mention it.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.716
Feel free to visit any time.

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:48.956
-Definitely!

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:52.966
♪♪

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:56.966
-[Caine]: [offscreen] Congratulations,
my little ironclad waffle cones!

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:59.626
You've taken the PACIFIST ROUTE,

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:02.456
and you should be proud
of what good people you are.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.065
Unfortunately,
we still need to wait

00:16:04.089 --> 00:16:06.190
until your other teammates
finish their adventure

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:08.666
before I can grant you
permission to leave.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.946
-I wonder how long that'll be?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.970
[water dripping]

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.756
-[Kinger]: Not really typical
of what you'd think Hell would be.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:17.956
-We…

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:21.076
are LITERALLY in Hell right now.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.716
HELL!

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.026
Of course I'd be in Hell.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.196
How could I not be
in literal Hell right now?

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:28.576
-[Kinger]: Just try to stay calm.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:31.200
I'm sure Caine included a way to escape.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.970
Hold on.

00:16:39.981 --> 00:16:41.980
[soft rushing]

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.140
Let me try something.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:53.626
Hey, there's actually
a staircase down there.

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.406
It could be a way out.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:58.636
Maybe it'll work for us
since we still have our bodies?

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.886
Though, I'm worried about
what that tape said earlier.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.980
-I'm just gonna try going fast.
-[Kinger]: Wait, Pomni!

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:07.966
-[grunts]

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:09.966
[dark music plays]

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:12.946
♪♪

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.186
-[Kinger]: Pomni!

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:19.336
♪♪

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.660
-[distorted voice]
[cackling]

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:26.290
Freeeeedooooom.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:27.756
-[Kinger]: Pomni!

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:31.676
♪♪

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:32.847
-[cackling]
-[Kinger]: Hey!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.980
You get out of her,
you damn evil souls!

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:38.870
-How's your wife, Kinger?

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:40.966
[coughs]

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.676
[normal voice] [coughs]
-[Kinger]: Hey.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.846
You all right there?
-[panting]

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.786
No.

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:51.346
-[Kinger]: I'm guessing
the souls are attracted to living things.

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:53.980
Just want a vessel
to be able to leave with.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:55.956
Man…

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:59.656
Seven years of computer science
for this, huh?

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.364
[chuckles]
-Why?

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:06.056
Every day I spend here
is one nightmare after the next!

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.636
I knew it would end up like this!

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:08.586
He --

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:10.630
He just wants me to suffer.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:13.606
I really am in Hell.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.116
-[Kinger]: Don't say that.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.596
You're not in --

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:18.956
Well, I-I guess we are technically in --

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:20.956
Eh, forget about that.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:24.990
How about we just relax for a bit
while nothing's chasing us?

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.980
-[sobbing quietly]

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:38.700
-[Kinger]: It was my fault
we went down this path, wasn't it?

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:42.980
I'm really sorry for that.

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:47.466
-Why have you been
acting so different lately?

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:48.956
-[Kinger]: [chuckles]

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:50.980
I have, haven't I?

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:54.946
I'm normally not too good with memories.

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:58.276
But being surrounded by darkness always…

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:00.600
brings me back to a certain time.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:04.456
Right after my wife had --

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.296
had abstracted…

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.506
I don't recall the exact string of events,

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:10.980
but we both ended up in the fort together.

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:13.560
And it was dark.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.980
The darkness seemed
to calm her down a bit.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.536
The harsh, jagged edges smoothed out,

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:23.980
and she didn't seem aggravated anymore.

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:26.866
She wasn't the same as before,

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.946
but she was calm enough

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:31.636
to touch one last time…

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.770
before she got sent to the cellar.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:39.786
I'm always taken back to that moment
when engulfed in darkness.

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:41.066
-You had a wife?

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:42.946
Like, here in the circus?

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:44.296
-[Kinger]: Yeah.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.486
She was funny, creative --

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.956
really into entomology.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.980
I used to hate bugs, but…

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.966
…she somehow got me to like them.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:57.246
[chuckles] It's not the most
cheerful memory, but…

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:59.990
it's one I at least have control over.

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:06.226
I know how it can feel in this…

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:07.630
circus.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:11.126
Sometimes it all just feels…

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.340
pointless.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:13.970
-Yeah.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.580
-[Kinger]: But it's not.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.000
Not if you have people who care about you.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.330
Good memories can do a lot.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.560
Hold onto them.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:28.640
And cherish the people around you.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:32.440
You never know when they'll be gone.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:37.696
In this world,
the worst thing you can do is…

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:40.980
make someone think
they're not wanted or loved.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.520
-I'm glad you're here with me.

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:57.980
-[Kinger]: You know, I've been
thinking about that last tape.

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:01.786
He said, “The next breath
you take down there…

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:03.736
will be your last.”

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:07.000
Maybe we can get through
if we don't breathe.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:11.856
-I'm not very good at holding my breath.

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.356
-[Kinger]: Well…

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:15.236
How about we try…

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:16.786
not thinking about it?

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.586
[hopeful music plays]

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:19.596
-[stammers]

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:22.816
♪♪

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:26.766
If we leave and we go back to the circus…

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:29.416
you're just gonna go back to being crazy.

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:32.576
You're not gonna remember any of this.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:33.906
Are you?

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:35.620
-[Kinger]: Don't worry about me.

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:38.576
As long as you remember it,

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:39.970
things will be okay.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:43.686
You're very strong, Pomni.

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:47.036
And I know you'll be able
to get through this.

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:49.036
Just hold onto me.

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:50.990
We'll get through it together.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.306
You ready?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:22:28.016
♪♪

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:29.476
-Oh, Pomni! Kinger!

00:22:29.500 --> 00:22:31.776
Are you guys okay? Was it scary?

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:34.330
-I'm fine, actually.

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:37.630
What happened up here?

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:40.276
-Uh, don't worry about that.

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:42.806
-[Kinger]: Pomni was very brave.

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:45.560
At least, I think she was.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:47.096
Were you?

00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:48.720
-Something like that.

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:51.867
Hey, Ragatha.

00:22:51.891 --> 00:22:54.526
-Yeah?
-I just want to say…

00:22:54.550 --> 00:22:57.356
[sighs] Thanks for always being
concerned about me.

00:22:57.380 --> 00:23:00.096
I feel like, through everything,

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:03.360
I haven't really been
appreciative enough about that.

00:23:03.930 --> 00:23:04.896
-O-Oh!

00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:06.456
Thank you, Pomni.

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.166
I just want to make sure
you're doin' all right.

00:23:09.190 --> 00:23:11.006
You know, we care about you.

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:13.500
-Did you remember to get my comedy mask?

00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:16.006
-[bonk!]

00:23:16.030 --> 00:23:18.676
-And -- And now,
I-I'm just starting to wonder

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:20.676
if the "Wild West" was…

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:23.320
e-even a real direction at all.

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:24.636
Whoopsie-daisy!

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.846
Looks like everybody completed
the adventure and they're coming home!

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:30.090
Quick, pretend we weren't
having a therapy session!

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:32.606
-[Zooble]: Okay?

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:35.760
-Welcome back, my meowing milkmaids!

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:38.710
-Don't ever call us that again.

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:44.456
Heh, so, what was it like
being stuck with the nutcase?

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:47.420
-It wasn't that bad, actually.

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:53.905
♪♪

00:23:56.277 --> 00:23:59.246
[upbeat, jazzy music plays]

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:21.020
♪♪

00:24:21.044 --> 00:24:22.954
[Captioned by Foulweather Studios]

00:24:22.978 --> 00:24:34.980
♪♪

